Spotify Connect plugin for Kalinka
=================================

This architecture-independent package installs the Python wheel under
/opt/kalinka/wheels. The kalinka-server-restart dpkg trigger asks the server
to restart; Kalinka's bootstrap then installs the wheel into its managed
environment. The plugin is disabled by default.

Before enabling Spotify:

* Install the matching SDK 3.5, server and renderer streaming support described
  in docs/core-compatibility.md in the source repository. SDK 3.5 alone is not
  sufficient; the server and renderer must support unfinished HTTP streams.
* Build/install librespot 0.8.0 with the Kalinka pipe bridge for the server's
  architecture, then set Spotify's executable setting to its absolute path.
  scripts/build-librespot.sh builds the pinned implementation, and
  scripts/verify-librespot.py verifies its output. A stock librespot executable
  is incompatible. The capability probe must include "volume": true,
  "reconnect": true and "suspend": true for volume sync and resuming after a
  queue handoff while keeping Kalinka selected in Spotify;
  rebuild older bridge versions when upgrading.
  This .deb contains the Python plugin, not a native binary.
* Select a renderer through Kalinka, enable Spotify Connect, and pair using
  the Spotify app with a Premium account.

Removal uninstalls the plugin from /opt/kalinka/venv using Kalinka's standard
prerm hook. Upgrades leave the existing installation in place until bootstrap
installs the new wheel. The package does not delete account credentials or
configuration, and it does not install a separate Spotify systemd service.

Build and operation instructions:
https://github.com/Kalinka-Player/kalinka-plugin-spotify
